-- title:
--   A verifier-register matrix acts correctly on every workspace fiber
-- statement:
--   Fix a G₂ verifier V, an arbitrary complex matrix M on its verifier-wire basis, and a workspace assignment s(j,c) depending on the index j and certificate c. If K_s embeds the corresponding logical basis states, physical placement of M on the verifier wires agrees with its logical action:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{physicalCall}(M)K_s
--      =K_s\operatorname{logicalCall}(M).
--   $$
--
--   The result is linear algebra for an arbitrary M; it assumes neither unitarity nor clean workspace. Applying it to the verifier unitary and its adjoint supplies the two quantum calls inside SELECT.
-- source:
